WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:01.680
Speaker 1: t said.

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:02.680
OK, join the discussion at David Pakman dotcom
slash Reddit.

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:03.680
That's already it.

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:06.339
Is Joe Biden abandoning the promised public
option.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:14.270
CNBC is now reporting that Joe Biden's new
American families plan does not include the

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:19.600
promised expansion of Medicare eligibility,
and it doesn't include a provision allowing

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.740
the program to negotiate prices directly with
drug companies.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:29.100
Dozens of Democratic lawmakers, CNBC rights
have urged Biden to include these provisions

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:32.189
in the second piece of his economic recovery
plan.

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:37.610
Biden's plan would make permanent premium
cuts for people buying insurance on the individual

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.230
market.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:47.070
Key Democrats are aiming to include a public
option bill or create a separate one now that

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:50.500
Joe Biden is not including it in his recovery
plan.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:57.040
Democratic Senators Patty Murray and Congressman
Frank Palone are going to write a bill to

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.070
create a public option.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:04.780
President Joe Biden did run on expanding the
public insurance market, but this is not in

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:06.080
any of his plans.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:13.150
So far, Republicans have exposed every effort,
have opposed every effort to expand government

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:15.080
managed health care.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:19.420
Democrats would likely have to look at doing
this either via a budget reconciliation bill

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:22.400
to pass it without Republican support, because
you're not going to get Republican support

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:29.060
for a public option or convincing Joe Biden
to put it in one of his plans, including possibly

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:31.190
the American families plan.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:35.330
There are lots of Democrats absolutely furious
with Joe Biden for not including this.

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:36.330
And I understand that.

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:40.369
And I'm with them now, you know that on this
program.

00:01:40.369 --> 00:01:46.810
We are pragmatic and I would like to see the
promised public option done now.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.420
I would like to see it done last month.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:52.509
I would have like to see it done when Obamacare
was first put together.

00:01:52.509 --> 00:01:59.630
I could understand if you said to me the inclusion
of the public option will never pass if you

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:01.250
make it part of this bill.

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:03.290
And so it makes sense for Joe Biden not to
include it.

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:04.640
I'm just not convinced of that yet.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:11.480
I have not seen evidence that if Democrats
hold firm and go to Joe Biden and say, listen,

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:16.590
Joe, Republicans don't want the public option,
OK, we're going to need to pass it via a budget

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:17.590
reconciliation.

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:20.809
If we're to do it outside of this, let's just
include it.

00:02:20.809 --> 00:02:21.930
Let's just include it now.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:26.930
And if we do this all via budget reconciliation,
then we get the public option done and let's

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:30.420
actually put Republicans in a position to
vote against all of this stuff.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:38.969
Now, the counter would be if you don't have
all 50 Democrats on board in the Senate.

00:02:38.969 --> 00:02:41.879
Then it's not going to pass either way because
you're not going to get a single Republican

00:02:41.879 --> 00:02:42.879
vote.

00:02:42.879 --> 00:02:46.269
So this is one of those situations where there's
truth to both sides.

00:02:46.269 --> 00:02:50.319
Do I believe that if Joe Biden doesn't do
the public option now, he never does it?

00:02:50.319 --> 00:02:54.400
No, I think it's possible that Joe Biden would
try to do it later on.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.760
But why wait?

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:56.760
Why wait?

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:59.569
There is no better time than now to do something.

00:02:59.569 --> 00:03:03.620
And remember, the public option was the starting
negotiating point with Obamacare in 2010.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:06.120
Should we should have had a better 2009?

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:10.709
Whenever the negotiations started, we should
have had a starting point that was far more

00:03:10.709 --> 00:03:12.739
progressive with Obamacare.

00:03:12.739 --> 00:03:15.730
The first thing to go was the public option
with Obamacare.

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:17.719
Is it possible Joe Biden will do this later?

00:03:17.719 --> 00:03:18.760
Sure, yeah.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:19.760
Maybe.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:20.760
Let's just do it right now.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.200
But you've got to have all 50 Democrats on
board.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.969
It is not completely clear to me that you
have them.

00:03:25.969 --> 00:03:30.040
So are the criticisms fair that it should
be done now?

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.269
Absolutely.

00:03:31.269 --> 00:03:36.599
Is the criticism fair that this is evidence
Biden is permanently abandoning the public

00:03:36.599 --> 00:03:37.599
option?

00:03:37.599 --> 00:03:38.599
No, we can't say that yet.

00:03:38.599 --> 00:03:40.889
We're four months into a four year term.

00:03:40.889 --> 00:03:44.980
That being said, my preference would be to
do this right now.

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:50.849
There is no reason to wait unless you don't
have all 50 Democrats on board.

00:03:50.849 --> 00:03:51.930
You've got to fight for their votes.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:54.459
You have to negotiate with them.

00:03:54.459 --> 00:03:56.569
If we find out.

00:03:56.569 --> 00:04:00.809
That it is three Democratic senators that
don't want the public option, and were it

00:04:00.809 --> 00:04:04.169
not for them, you could do all of this via
budget reconciliation.

00:04:04.169 --> 00:04:06.290
I would say you've got to bring those three
people.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:09.010
Joe Biden brags about being able to negotiate.

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:11.389
He brags about being able to get deals done
with the other side.

00:04:11.389 --> 00:04:13.349
We'll get a deal done with your own side.

00:04:13.349 --> 00:04:16.730
Get those three hypothetical senators who
don't want the public option in the American

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.310
families plan.

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:21.900
Bring them to the White House and convince
them, negotiate with them.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:27.960
Do the thing that you ran on being able to
do as a diplomat and an elected official and

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:30.180
a dealmaker in the Senate for a long time.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:31.449
Could it be done in three months?

00:04:31.449 --> 00:04:32.449
Could it be done in six months?

00:04:32.449 --> 00:04:34.210
Could it be done in 2022?

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:35.539
Sure.

00:04:35.539 --> 00:04:37.590
But I would like to see it done right now.

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:42.360
And until I see evidence that it couldn't
be done right now, I believe we need to continue

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:43.500
pushing for it to be done.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.590
Now, many of you will write in and say, David,
this is pathetic.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:48.860
You just got to do Medicare for all.

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:52.060
Many Democratic senators don't support Medicare
for all, and neither does Joe Biden.

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:54.310
Medicare for all is not going to happen right
now.

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:59.520
OK, so what's on the table is can we get a
public option done?

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:05.020
An idea would be get some Democrats to lobby
for Medicare for all in this bill and negotiate

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:06.020
to a public option.

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:07.780
I would be open to that.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:11.030
But I don't want is something that has no
chance of passing.

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:13.639
If that's the case, we don't know that to
be the case yet.

00:05:13.639 --> 00:05:17.490
If there's no chance of passing, there's no
point in holding this bill up indefinitely.

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:19.240
But I've not seen the work done yet.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:23.349
That proves to me you can't force a public
option into this bill right now.

00:05:23.349 --> 00:05:27.300
If you disagree with me, let me know and we'll
have more coverage of the coverage of this

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:32.009
on our Instagram page, which you can find
at David Pakman show on Instagram.

00:05:32.009 --> 00:07:22.370
While you're there, follow me on Instagram
at David Pakman.

